Marijke, Rajeev,

Apologies for coming back only today. I did not want to put a number in writing
before I could tie it back to the trial balance.

1. The validated credit note impact on net revenue for FY26 is
INR 3,11,20,000, that is INR 3.11 Cr. Period covered is 01-Apr-2025 to
31-Mar-2026, the full FY26, not a part year.

2. That figure is 1,206 documents, all of them CN_TYPE = RATE_DIFF or
OFF_INV_ADJ. Those are the two types that move the revenue line, the rate
difference cases and the off invoice adjustments.

3. FY26 Credit Notes in total are 9,318 documents and 31,204 lines out of
ORION. The remaining 8,112 documents are DAMAGE, RETURN and SCHEME, INR 43.70 Cr,
and those settle against provisions or come back through the scheme accrual, so
they do not sit in the 3.11 Cr. (The 1,206 count is as at Friday night's
extract. If a July document is backdated into FY26 it will move by a few.)

4. On why this is different from the number in the May pack. That was a quick
sizing, done in a day, to give the programme an order of magnitude. It covered
April 2025 to December 2025 only, so the whole of FY26 Q4 was missing from it,
and it left out the OFF_INV_ADJ type completely. Put Jan to Mar back in, add
OFF_INV_ADJ, and you arrive at 3.11 Cr. The May number was not wrong for what it
was, it was wrong for what it got used for, which is my fault as much as
anybody's.

5. What the revalidation actually covered. My team pulled every FY26 credit
note document from ORION, matched them by document number and party code to the
AR side, classifed them by CN_TYPE and then tied the revenue affecting types
back to the FY26 trial balance line by line. Where a document could not be tied
it has been left out of the 1,206.

6. On the question of since when. VAR-005 "Credit notes absent from warehouse"
has been on the variance register since 24-Apr-2026 and it is open with me as
owner. So it is not a new item. What is new as of today is that the number is
firm.

7. Tracker: I have asked for VAR-005 to be updated with the validated figure.
The summary sheet will round to 3.10 Cr, the detail sheet carries the full
3,11,20,000, please quote the detail sheet if it is going anywhere near Group.

Marijke, on the walk, I can have it by month and by credit note type. Tell me
whether you want it in INR or in EUR at the budget rate and I will send it in
whichever template Wei Lin needs.

Regards,
Shalini

